<title>HONG KONG: Air Hong Kong changes Manchester handling agent.</title>
<headline>Air Hong Kong changes Manchester handling agent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>AHK Air Hong Kong Ltd, the territory's all cargo airline, has begun using a new cargo handling agent for its UK flights to and from Manchester, the airline's chief operating officer Stanley Hui told Reuters.</p>
<p>AHK has also signed a new three year agreement with the London Cargo Group which has been handling the airline's cargo at Heathrow since 1990, Hui added.</p>
<p>MANCargo Handling, which is part of the London Cargo Group, a division of BOC Distribution Services, took over from AHK's previous Manchester agent Servisair on November 25.</p>
<p>AHK is 75 percent owned by Cathay Pacific Airways Limited.</p>
